# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# golder config files (may contain plaintext API keys)
config.toml
**/config.toml
.golder/

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# macOS Finder metadata
.DS_Store

.loop-state.json

# Compiled binary (go build ./cmd/golder produces ./golder)
/golder

# Local build output (scratch binaries built by hand during development).
# Nothing here is produced by CI: .github/workflows/build.yml writes to
# release/, which is ignored below.
/.build/

# Reference checkouts pulled by hand while working (the MIT-licensed
# bash-classify rule table, used to seed internal/judge/risk.go). Never
# committed and never built: they are reading material, and a stale copy in the
# repository would be a second source of truth for data that lives in Go now.
/.ref-*/

# goreleaser output
/dist/
# build workflow output (macOS/Linux archives + checksums)
/release/
.graph_state
graph.html
